{title: Day Is Dying in the West}
{artist: Mary A. Lathbury / William F. Sherwin}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 145}
{time: 6/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Pilgrim Hymnal (Boston, Massachusetts: Pilgrim Press, 1958), # 45)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Day is dying in the west;
[G]Heav’n is touching earth with rest;
[D7]Wait and worship while the [G]night
[D7]Sets the [G]evening [Em]lamps [A7]a[D]light
[G]Through [D]all__[A7]__ the [D]sky.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Holy, holy, holy, Lord__[D7]__ God of [G]Hosts!
[C]Heav’n and earth are [G]full of Thee!
[D7]Heav’n and earth are [G]praising Thee,
[C]O [G]Lord__[D7]__ most [G]high!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Lord of life, beneath the dome
[G]Of the universe, Thy home,
[D7]Gather us who seek Thy [G]face
[D7]To the [G]fold of [Em]Thy [A7]em[D]brace,
[G]For [D]Thou__[A7]__ art [D]nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]While the deepening shadows fall,
[G]Heart of love enfolding all,
[D7]Through the glory and the [G]grace
[D7]Of the [G]stars that [Em]veil [A7]Thy [D]face,
[G]Our [D]hearts__[A7]__ a[D]scend.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]When forever from our sight
[G]Pass the stars, the day, the night,
[D7]Lord of angels, on our [G]eyes
[D7]Let e[G]ternal [Em]morn[A7]ing [D]rise
[G]And [D]sha__[A7]__dows [D]end.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
